# 🩸 Salvage and scratch left in the working tree, 2026-08-28.
# `.git-BROKEN-2026-08-04/` is a rescued git directory — hundreds of loose
# objects, its own refs, and a `config`. A `git add -A` during the 0.5.1 release
# swept the whole thing into a commit and pushed it before it was caught.
# Untracked-but-present files are invisible in a diff review and land in the
# next `-A`, so they are ignored here rather than trusted to be noticed again.
.git-BROKEN-*/
*.prototype-unported
